{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_r2_peer_confidence.py' -TotalCount 160; Get-Content -LiteralPath 'AdaRES/ipdn/model_paper5/adares_b4_query_competition/dec.py' -TotalCount 240\"","aggregated_output":"import argparse\r\nimport json\r\nimport statistics\r\nimport sys\r\nimport types\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport gorilla\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\r\n\r\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\r\nfrom ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\r\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\r\n\r\n\r\ndef predictor(self, scan_ids, object_idss, ann_ids, out, superpoints,\r\n              gt_pmasks, gt_spmasks, fps_seed_sp):\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for index, target in enumerate(gt_pmasks):\r\n        valid = ~out[\"batch_mask\"][index]\r\n        masks = out[\"masks\"][index, :, valid].sigmoid()\r\n        area = masks.sum(-1)\r\n        intersection = masks @ masks.T\r\n        overlap = intersection / (\r\n            area[:, None] + area[None, :] - intersection\r\n        ).clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        overlap.fill_diagonal_(0)\r\n        confidence = F.softmax(out[\"indis\"][index], dim=-1)[:, 1]\r\n        # Frozen control: the same peer confidence assigned to shifted query IDs.\r\n        null_confidence = confidence.roll(1)\r\n        support = overlap @ confidence / overlap.sum(-1).clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        null_support = overlap @ null_confidence / overlap.sum(-1).clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        plain_support = overlap.mean(-1)\r\n        product = confidence * support\r\n        null_product = confidence * null_support\r\n        plain_product = confidence * plain_support\r\n        hard_masks = out[\"masks\"][index].sigmoid().gt(0.5)[:, superpoints]\r\n        truth = target.gt(0.5).to(hard_masks.device)\r\n        ious = (hard_masks & truth).sum(-1).float() / (\r\n            (hard_masks | truth).sum(-1).clamp_min(1).float()\r\n        )\r\n        selected, oracle = int(confidence.argmax()), int(ious.argmax())\r\n        rows.append({\r\n            \"scene\": self.probe_scene,\r\n            \"selected\": selected,\r\n            \"oracle\": oracle,\r\n            \"selected_iou\": float(ious[selected]),\r\n            \"oracle_iou\": float(ious[oracle]),\r\n            \"selected_support\": float(support[selected]),\r\n            \"oracle_support\": float(support[oracle]),\r\n            \"selected_null\": float(null_support[selected]),\r\n            \"oracle_null\": float(null_support[oracle]),\r\n            \"selected_plain\": float(plain_support[selected]),\r\n            \"oracle_plain\": float(plain_support[oracle]),\r\n            \"support_iou\": float(ious[support.argmax()]),\r\n            \"product_iou\": float(ious[product.argmax()]),\r\n            \"null_product_iou\": float(ious[null_product.argmax()]),\r\n            \"plain_product_iou\": float(ious[plain_product.argmax()]),\r\n            \"product_flip\": int(product.argmax()) != selected,\r\n            \"null_product_flip\": int(null_product.argmax()) != selected,\r\n            \"plain_product_flip\": int(plain_product.argmax()) != selected,\r\n        })\r\n    return {\"rows\": rows}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--scenes\", type=int, default=64)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=0)\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\r\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\r\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\r\n    data_cfg = cfg.data.train.copy()\r\n    data_cfg.training = False\r\n    data_cfg.aug = False\r\n    data_cfg.with_elastic = False\r\n    data_cfg.lang_num_max = 32\r\n    dataset = build_dataset(data_cfg, get_root_logger())\r\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\r\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\r\n    loaded = model.load_state_dict(checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint), strict=False)\r\n    allowed = {\"text_encoder.embeddings.position_ids\",\r\n               \"text_encoder.embeddings.token_type_ids\"}\r\n    if loaded.missing_keys or set(loaded.unexpected_keys) - allowed:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Checkpoint mismatch: {loaded}\")\r\n    model.eval()\r\n    model.predict_by_feat = types.MethodType(predictor, model)\r\n    rows = []\r\n    repeat_mismatch = 0\r\n    for scene in range(min(args.scenes, len(dataset))):\r\n        model.probe_scene = scene\r\n        batch = dataset.collate_fn([dataset[scene]])\r\n        with torch.no_grad():\r\n            base = model(batch, mode=\"predict\")[\"rows\"]\r\n            repeat = model(batch, mode=\"predict\")[\"rows\"]\r\n        repeat_mismatch += sum(\r\n            a[\"selected\"] != b[\"selected\"] or a[\"oracle\"] != b[\"oracle\"]\r\n            or abs(a[\"selected_support\"] - b[\"selected_support\"]) > 1e-4\r\n            for a, b in zip(base, repeat)\r\n        )\r\n        rows.extend(base)\r\n    errors = [r for r in rows if r[\"oracle_iou\"] - r[\"selected_iou\"] > 0.05]\r\n    result = {\r\n        \"scenes\": min(args.scenes, len(dataset)),\r\n        \"expressions\": len(rows),\r\n        \"material_errors\": len(errors),\r\n        \"repeat_mismatch\": repeat_mismatch,\r\n        \"oracle_higher_support\": sum(\r\n            r[\"oracle_support\"] > r[\"selected_support\"] for r in errors),\r\n        \"oracle_higher_null\": sum(\r\n            r[\"oracle_null\"] > r[\"selected_null\"] for r in errors),\r\n        \"oracle_higher_plain\": sum(\r\n            r[\"oracle_plain\"] > r[\"selected_plain\"] for r in errors),\r\n        \"indicator_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"support_only_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"support_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"product_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"product_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"null_product_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"null_product_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"plain_product_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"plain_product_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"product_flips\": sum(r[\"product_flip\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"null_product_flips\": sum(r[\"null_product_flip\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"plain_product_flips\": sum(r[\"plain_product_flip\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"peak_reserved_gib\": torch.cuda.max_memory_reserved() / 2**30,\r\n        \"rows\": rows,\r\n    }\r\n    Path(args.output).write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in result.items() if k != \"rows\"}))\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn as nn\r\nfrom .sample_model import SamplingModule\r\nimport ipdn.torch.nn_new.functional as F\r\nfrom ipdn.torch.nn_new import MultiheadAttention\r\n\r\nclass ThreeLayerMLP(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"A 3-layer MLP with normalization and dropout.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, dim, out_dim):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, dim, 1, bias=False),\r\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(dim),\r\n            nn.ReLU(),\r\n            nn.Dropout(0.3),\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, dim, 1, bias=False),\r\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(dim),\r\n            nn.ReLU(),\r\n            nn.Dropout(0.3),\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, out_dim, 1)\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x):\r\n        \"\"\"Forward pass, x can be (B, dim, N).\"\"\"\r\n        return self.net(x)\r\n\r\nclass CrossAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model=256, nhead=8, dropout=0.0):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.attn = MultiheadAttention(d_model, nhead, dropout=dropout, batch_first=True)\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\r\n        self._reset_parameters()\r\n        self.nhead = nhead\r\n\r\n    def _reset_parameters(self):\r\n        for p in self.parameters():\r\n            if p.dim() > 1:\r\n                nn.init.xavier_uniform_(p)\r\n\r\n    def with_pos_embed(self, tensor, pos):\r\n        return tensor if pos is None else tensor + pos\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, source, query, batch_mask=None, attn_mask=None, pe=None, att_weights=None):\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        source (B, N_p, d_model)\r\n        batch_offsets Tensor (b, n_p)\r\n        query Tensor (b, n_q, d_model)\r\n        attn_masks Tensor (b, n_q, n_p)\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        B = query.shape[0]\r\n        query = self.with_pos_embed(query, pe)\r\n        k = v = source\r\n        if attn_mask is not None:\r\n            attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, self.nhead, 1, 1).view(B*self.nhead, query.shape[1], k.shape[1])\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(query, k, v, key_padding_mask=batch_mask, attn_mask=attn_mask, att_weights =att_weights)  # (1, 100, d_model)\r\n        else:\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(query, k, v, key_padding_mask=batch_mask, att_weights =att_weights)\r\n        self.dropout(output)\r\n        output = output + query\r\n        self.norm(output)\r\n\r\n        return output, output_weight, src_weight # (b, n_q, d_model), (b, n_q, n_v)\r\n\r\nclass SelfAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model=256, nhead=8, dropout=0.0, glu = False):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.attn = MultiheadAttention(\r\n            d_model,\r\n            nhead,\r\n            dropout=dropout,\r\n            batch_first=True,\r\n        )\r\n        self.nhead = nhead\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\r\n        self.glu = glu\r\n        if glu:\r\n            self.glu_p = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)\r\n            self.glu_g = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)\r\n\r\n    def with_pos_embed(self, tensor, pos):\r\n        return tensor if pos is None else tensor + pos\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x, x_mask=None, attn_mask=None, pe=None, norm=True, att_weights=None):\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        x Tensor (b, n_w, c)\r\n        x_mask Tensor (b, n_w)\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        B = x.shape[0]\r\n        q = k = self.with_pos_embed(x, pe)\r\n        if attn_mask is not None:\r\n            attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, self.nhead, 1, 1).view(B*self.nhead, q.shape[1], k.shape[1])\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(q, k, x, key_padding_mask=x_mask, attn_mask=attn_mask, att_weights =att_weights)  # (1, 100, d_model)\r\n        else:\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(q, k, x, key_padding_mask=x_mask, att_weights =att_weights)\r\n        if self.glu:\r\n            output = self.glu_p(output) * (self.glu_g(output).sigmoid())\r\n        output = self.dropout(output) + x\r\n        if norm: output = self.norm(output)\r\n        return output\r\n\r\nclass FFN(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model, hidden_dim, dropout=0.0, activation_fn='relu'):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        if activation_fn == 'relu':\r\n            self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n                nn.Linear(d_model, hidden_dim),\r\n                nn.ReLU(),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, d_model),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n            )\r\n        elif activation_fn == 'gelu':\r\n            self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n                nn.Linear(d_model, hidden_dim),\r\n                nn.GELU(),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, d_model),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n            )\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x, norm=True):\r\n        output = self.net(x)\r\n        output = output + x\r\n        if norm: output = self.norm(output)\r\n        return output\r\n\r\nclass MLP(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\" Very simple multi-layer perceptron (also called FFN)\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, input_dim, hidden_dim, output_dim, num_layers):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.num_layers = num_layers\r\n        h = [hidden_dim] * (num_layers - 1)\r\n        self.layers = nn.ModuleList(nn.Linear(n, k) for n, k in zip([input_dim] + h, h + [output_dim]))\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x):\r\n        for i, layer in enumerate(self.layers):\r\n            x = F.relu(layer(x)) if i < self.num_layers - 1 else layer(x)\r\n        return x\r\n\r\n\r\nclass QueryCompetitionIndicator(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"Predict confidence from a query and its overlapping competitors.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.query_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.evidence_norm = nn.LayerNorm(3 * d_model + 1)\r\n        self.head = nn.Sequential(\r\n            nn.Linear(3 * d_model + 1, d_model),\r\n            nn.GELU(),\r\n            nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),\r\n            nn.GELU(),\r\n            nn.Linear(d_model, 2),\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, query, pred_masks, batch_mask):\r\n        valid = (~batch_mask).unsqueeze(1).to(pred_masks.dtype)\r\n        probabilities = pred_masks.sigmoid() * valid\r\n        areas = probabilities.sum(-1)\r\n        intersection = torch.einsum(\r\n            'bim,bjm->bij', probabilities, probabilities\r\n        )\r\n        union = areas.unsqueeze(-1) + areas.unsqueeze(1) - intersection\r\n        overlap = intersection / union.clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        diagonal = torch.eye(\r\n            overlap.shape[-1], dtype=torch.bool, device=overlap.device\r\n        ).unsqueeze(0)\r\n        overlap = overlap.masked_fill(diagonal, 0.0)\r\n\r\n        competition = overlap / overlap.sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        normalized_query = self.query_norm(query)\r\n        context = torch.einsum('bij,bjd->bid', competition, normalized_query)\r\n        max_overlap = overlap.max(-1).values.unsqueeze(-1)\r\n        evidence = torch.cat(\r\n            [\r\n                normalized_query,\r\n                context,\r\n                normalized_query - context,\r\n                max_overlap,\r\n            ],\r\n            dim=-1,\r\n        )\r\n        return self.head(self.evidence_norm(evidence))\r\n    \r\n    \r\nclass DEC(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    in_channels List[int] (4,) [64,96,128,160]\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    def __init__(\r\n        self,\r\n        num_layer=6,\r\n        num_class=256,\r\n        in_channel=32,\r\n        d_model=256,\r\n        nhead=8,\r\n        hidden_dim=1024,\r\n        dropout=0.0,\r\n        activation_fn='relu',\r\n        iter_pred=False,\r\n        attn_mask=False,\r\n        sampling_module=None,\r\n        kernel='top1',\r\n        global_feat='mean',\r\n        lang_att=False,\r\n        contrastive_align_loss=False,\r\n        num_proposal_fine=512,\r\n        num_proposal_query = [128,64,32,16,8,4],\r\n        num_proposal_query_inst = [128,64,32,16,8,4]\r\n    ):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.num_layer = num_layer\r\n        self.num_class = num_class\r\n        self.d_model = d_model\r\n        self.input_proj = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(in_channel, d_model), nn.LayerNorm(d_model), nn.ReLU())\r\n        \r\n        self.input_proj_2d = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(1024, d_model*2),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model*2, d_model),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))#clip\r\n        self.sum_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        \r\n        self.lang_att = lang_att\r\n        self.contrastive_align_loss = contrastive_align_loss\r\n\r\n        H = 768\r\n        self.lang_proj = nn.Linear(H, d_model)\r\n        self.lang_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        \r\n        if sampling_module is not None:\r\n            self.sampling_module = SamplingModule(**sampling_module)\r\n        else:\r\n            self.sampling_module = None\r\n        self.num_proposal_fine = num_proposal_fine\r\n        self.num_proposal_query = num_proposal_query\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md','pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-220200.md','pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-220200.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"Get-Content: \r\nLine |\r\n   2 |  Get-Content -LiteralPath 'pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md',' …\r\n     |  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n     | 找不到路径“pipeline/references/autonomous_design.md”，因为该路径不存在。\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 22:02 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 0.5020; B4-E30 0.5094; gap 0.0056. Goal constraints and bans checked: server-2 GPU0/1 only, one task per GPU, released backbone and project decoder, fixed B2/B4 continuation, full metric/resource reporting, no validation tuning.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Query competition | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below target |\n| Metric-IoU relabeling | Negative | G1 0.4980 | Do not repeat |\n| Matched-positive selection | Observational | R1 training positive-restricted oracle 0.89203 | Oracle label unavailable at inference |\n| Peer confidence | Negative | R2 frozen product 0.79612 vs B4 0.82254 | Strict repeats unstable |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061, G1 0.4980. R1 and R2 are native read-only probes, not trained experiments.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nTraining positive labels and mask quality disagree in both directions. A label-free, inference-available discriminator has not been demonstrated. Peer confidence alone has error association but degrades frozen selection, and the previous attention/topology/appearance routes remain rejected. Active queries, full latency and training peak memory are incomplete.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nR1 audited whether the standard supervision ceiling explains the mask/selection gap; it does not by itself specify a deployable confidence path. R2 tested a structurally distinct confidence communication rule with frozen nulls and was disconfirmed. Any future independent positive-evidence mechanism must be predeclared and pass native controls, backward, resources, independence and constraints.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-220200.md`.\n\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 22:02 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Active 0/2, admission budget 2. R1 tested the positive-label ceiling; R2 tested confidence propagation across overlapping peers.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nR1 found a large training positive-label mismatch and oracle-restricted headroom; supervision-derived positive membership cannot be used at inference, and G1/C1 already tested direct target/listwise routes unsuccessfully. R2 peer support beat a rotated control pairwise but frozen re-ranking declined by 0.0264 mIoU on the same training cohort and failed strict repeat consistency. No validation feature or weight scan.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo variant passes all six admission gates. R1 is an oracle-label audit with no inference-valid candidate; a future positive-evidence proposal requires independent motivation and native controls. R2 is rejected for this frozen propagation rule. Do not interpret label-filtered oracle ceilings as deployable results.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0/1 both idle at targeted query (0%, 1 MiB). GPU0 read-only probes finished; queue remains empty. No post-probe occupancy claim. Server-6 excluded.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed 64 training-scene R1/R2 native diagnostics and raw evidence.\n- [x] R1 positive/negative oracle ceiling; R2 cyclic-null/plain-overlap controls and frozen product.\n- [ ] Future independent mechanism: native matched controls, backward/training resources, independent model/config and tests.\n- [ ] No admission receipt, sync, queue update or training without all hard gates.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nTraining cohort is diagnostic. R1 positive labels leak training instance annotations; R2 had 30 strict repeated-readout mismatches and inferior frozen product. Inference memory is not training memory. No theoretical novelty claim.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nNo tuning-only, seed-repeat, ablation-only, banned or renamed-duplicate candidate was admitted. A positivity threshold or peer fusion weight scan would violate the goal; future mechanism must add a justified information path.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. R1 oracle-positive gating is inference-invalid; R2 frozen peer propagation was disconfirmed. No global exhaustion claim.\n\r\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
